course: dictionary
lesson: 14302
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have a serious meaning and a jokey meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. «Nuke» is one of these words. In news and history books it means a nuclear weapon, a bomb of enormous power. In everyday talk it can be slang, as in «Nuke the pizza», which means heat it in a microwave.
explain: Look at the words around the word. A history lesson about wars and nuclear bombs gives a serious meaning. A sentence about dinner, a microwave or a computer game gives a different one. Always ask: does this sentence sound serious or jokey? Then try the meaning you chose in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Slang words can also be informal, so people use them with friends, not in formal writing. Check the dictionary when you are unsure, because the same word can mean destroy, heat, or a weapon depending on who is speaking and why.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Nuke» (noun) means a nuclear weapon, a bomb of enormous power.
fact: «Nuke» (verb) can mean to attack a place with nuclear weapons.
fact: «Nuke» (slang) can mean to heat food in a microwave.
fact: «Nuke» (slang) can mean to destroy or delete something completely, such as a file in a computer game.
exercise: Mum says, «Nuke the leftover pizza for two minutes.» What does nuke mean here? | *Heat it in a microwave | Eat it cold | Cut it into small slices | Throw it in the bin
exercise: The history teacher says, «A nuke is a bomb of enormous power.» What is a nuke? | *A nuclear weapon | A type of cloud | A very small insect | A kind of pizza
exercise: Sam says, «I nuked my old save files to start the game again.» What does nuked suggest? | *Deleted them completely | Saved them carefully | Copied them to a friend | Printed them out
test: The news says a country could nuke another country. What does nuke mean here? | To write a letter to its leader | To give it a gift of food | To send it a birthday card | *To attack it with nuclear weapons
test: Which sentence uses nuke as jokey slang? | «Nukes are a serious danger to the world.» | «The nuke was the most powerful weapon of its time.» | «The treaty aims to stop nuclear weapons.» | *«Let's nuke the soup for lunch.»
exam: In «The news warned that a nuke could destroy a city», which meaning fits best? | A slow type of game | A cake covered in cream | A kind of shoe | *A nuclear weapon, a bomb of enormous power
